The UnB has consistently reached the finals of the SBC Programming Marathon, sometimes representing Brazil internationally. Despite efforts by professors to increase female participation, these were ineffective until the Meninas.comp project, which led to a rise in female competitors. Since 2022, five editions of the UnB's Female Programming Competition have been held exclusively for girls. The first edition in October 2022 involved a team of one professor and four students. Key steps included: 

- Promotion through banners and internal communication;
- A registration form to manage space limitations and pre-event emails for preparation;
- Question paper preparation by faculty experienced in internal competitions;
- Event management using an online judge (Codeforces) and a competition-like environment with balloons for problem-solving;
- Financial support from the Department of Computer Science, including coffee breaks and medals for winners.

